  "id": "COMPOUND:30124 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between 7-O-Methylmangiferin and Thrombopoietin, mediated through a series of targets that ultimately converge on Thrombopoietin. The drug appears to act as a target for multiple compounds, including MIP, Sophoradiol, and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, all of which are implicated in the regulation of thrombopoiesis. These targets are likely involved in signaling pathways that influence blood cell production, with Thrombopoietin serving as a key hormone in this process. The evidence supports a mechanism where 7-O-Methylmangiferin may modulate these pathways, potentially through direct or indirect interactions that enhance or inhibit the activity of Thrombopoietin. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 7-O-Methylmangiferin in the regulation of thrombopoiesis, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
